ll 2019 U.S. population.\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Counties were grouped according to four fixed poverty ranges, each covering approximately one quarter of the overall 2019 U.S. population.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Rates for specific age groups are reported as crude rates; other rates were age-adjusted to the year 2000 U.S. standard population.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Rates involving firearm homicide or suicide counts <20 are not presented because of concerns about statistical instability\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"this criterion ensures that relative SEs usually do not exceed 23% under the assumption that counts are Poisson-distributed\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"comparisons are nominal and do not involve formal statistical testing\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Rate comparisons between years refer to absolute differences unless relative (percentage) changes are indicated.\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"study_design\"]}", "type": "text"}]}